         <title><![CDATA[Ontario to table fall fiscal update next week as province continues to weather U.S. tariff impacts]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/toronto/ontario-fall-fiscal-update-announced-oct-29-9.7391410?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/f26e9b7d-146b-4f07-9291-65b0f7b4d77b,1774557939207/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C301%2C5772%2C3246%29%3B' alt='A man speaks at a podium with his hands up.' width='620' height='349' title='Finance minister Peter Bethlenfalvy speaks to reporters before tabling the provincial budget, at Queen’s Park, in Toronto, on March 26, 2026.'/><p>Finance Minister Peter Bethlenfalvy announced in a breakfast speech to the Canadian Club Thursday that he will table his government's fall economic statement next week, on Oct. 29. The document will provide an update on the province's finances and outline the next phase of his plan.</p>]]></description>
